    "summary": "Smoking St. Stephen > Midnight Hour and soulful Baby Blue",
    "blurb": "The second set rides a hot groove from Saint Stephen into Not Fade Away and In The Midnight Hour before closing with an emotionally resonant It's All Over Now Baby Blue. Jerry’s guitar tone is flawless and his vocals are unusually sweet on the acoustic numbers, while Pigpen adds church‑y organ depth. Highlights include Black Peter, Swing Low (Sweet Chariot) and a soaring acoustic set.",
    "review": "On June 4 1970 at the Fillmore West the Dead delivered a scorching second half that still feels fresh today. After a solid first set of roots‑rock and folk‑flavored numbers, they launched into a blistering Saint Stephen → Not Fade Away → In The Midnight Hour sequence that showcases tight drumming from Mickey and Bill and Jerry’s perfect‑tone lead work. Pigpen’s organ swells on the heartfelt It's All Over Now Baby Blue, complementing Jerry’s warm vocals. The acoustic interludes shine as well – Black Peter receives a sweet vocal treatment, and Swing Low (Sweet Chariot) glows with intimate group dynamics. Overall the night is marked by tight jams, seamless segues, and a balance of electric fire and acoustic warmth.",
